/-
  Kepler/Text/LP/W6Data — W6-A light LP certificate data root.

  Machine generated by `tools/gen_w6_lean.py`; do not edit.

  Carries the 19,715 graph certificate trees in light form (split shape +
  terminal precision/infeasible flags; constraint tables empty by W6-A
  contract). Import graph stays in the LP data layer: only
  Kepler.Text.LP.LPSchema / LPIds, never Kepler.Assembly.

  Accounting split: the 19,700 easy-batch graphs (23,640 terminals) are
  small enough for kernel `decide` counters; the 15 hard graphs (19,438
  terminals, single trees up to 9,080 leaves) carry dumper-literal counts
  (`hardTerminalCount` etc.) because kernel evaluation of `dfsTerminals`
  over those trees exceeded the build memory budget (evidence in
  W6A_REPORT.md). The 43,078 record-id reconciliation is fully
  kernel-checked in `Coverage.recordIds_eq_lpTerminalIds`.
-/
import Kepler.Text.LP.W6Data.Basic
import Kepler.Text.LP.W6Data.Shard00
import Kepler.Text.LP.W6Data.Shard01
import Kepler.Text.LP.W6Data.Shard02
